  "why": "Frozen behavior of clear_fence's READER half, captured before S3 deletes clear_fence.inspect and notice_expired_once. Arms in session/tests/test_clear_fence.py import them directly and stop testing anything at the delete, and no Python caller survives to act as a live oracle. Regenerate only by checking out the blob id above.",
  "malformed_vs_unreadable": "inspect returns `rec` at BOTH malformed exits (a dict whose since_epoch or ceiling_seconds is unusable) and `rec: null` ONLY when the file could not be read or parsed into a dict. A reader with one try/catch around the whole body collapses these, and a marker with a bad ceiling then loses the since/pid/nonce the Bash diagnostics print (lib.sh:445-452) -- a diagnostic that names the wedged clearer becomes one that says nothing.",
  "raised_is_an_observable": "A `raised` row means the incumbent exited nonzero. At the only door that calls notice_expired_once, `[ \"$rc\" -eq 0 ] || return 0` maps that to SUPPRESSED: no warning, no sidecar, indistinguishable from an already-noticed nonce. The port must reproduce the door's observable, not the traceback.",
